# Vitest tests (`tests/`)

New unit tests live under `tests/`, not colocated next to source. Mirror the module path under `src/` (`src/server/ai/foo.ts` → `tests/server/ai/foo.test.ts`).

## Stack

- Vitest (`npm test` / `npm run test:watch`); config is `vitest.config.mts`
- Import app code via `@/` (`@/server/ai/...`)
- Node environment; do not boot Next.js or hit live OpenRouter/Mongo

## Style

- Name files `*.test.ts`
- One `describe` per unit under test; `it` names state the behavior
- Reset module state in `afterEach` (e.g. `resetModelCooldowns()`)
- Mock I/O at the module boundary (`vi.mock("@/server/ai/openrouterClient")`); never call real APIs
- Prefer `rejects.toBeInstanceOf` / `toMatchObject` over catching by hand
- Fake time with `vi.useFakeTimers()` and restore in `afterEach`

```ts
// ❌ BAD — colocated, hits the network
// src/server/ai/completionService.test.ts
await fetch("https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models");

// ✅ GOOD — dedicated folder, mocked client
// tests/server/ai/completionService.test.ts
vi.mock("@/server/ai/openrouterClient", () => ({ default: { chat: { completions: { create: createMock } } } }));
```

Existing `src/**/*.test.ts` files may stay until moved; do not add new colocated specs.

## `tests/` vs `evals/`

`tests/` is CI-run, mocked, and free — it verifies code behavior (fallback logic, schemas, etc.). `evals/` is a separate, manual-only harness that makes real OpenRouter calls to grade the assistant's actual answers (factual accuracy, hallucination, tone, etc.) against the system prompt via an LLM judge. Run it with `npm run eval` (never in CI, never on save). See `evals/index.ts` for CLI flags and `evals/report.ts` for the generated report shape.
